                  "emoji": "🌸 🔴",
                  "label": "a picture"
                }
              },
              {
                "stage": "explain",
                "text": "Water-carrying tubes take water and mineral salts up from the roots to the leaves. Food-carrying tubes take food from the leaves to all parts of the plant."
              },
              {
                "stage": "apply",
                "text": "Your turn: A white flower is put in red-coloured water. After a day, the petals turn red. Why?",
                "interact": {
                  "kind": "check",
                  "prompt": "A white flower is put in red-coloured water. After a day, the petals turn red. Why?",
                  "visual": {
                    "kind": "letters",
                    "emoji": "🌸",
                    "label": "a picture"
                  },
                  "choices": [
                    "The red colour came from the air.",
                    "The flower made red food.",
                    "The water-carrying tubes carried the red water up."
                  ],
                  "answer": "The water-carrying tubes carried the red water up.",
                  "explain": "The coloured water went up the water-carrying tubes into the petals."
                }
              }
            ]
          },
